     ===================================================== -->
<div class="p10-banner">
    <div class="p10-phase-pill">Phase 10 · Torque-Driven Generator Test</div>
    <h1>Single-Generator <em>Torque Reciprocation Experiment</em></h1>
    <p>
        Phase 10 strips Phase 9 back to a testable core: one generator, mechanically coupled to the
        oil pan and driven by the combined torque of all six wheels and two steam rails.
        The scientific question — can a single steam-engine generator sustain its own boiler?
        Pressurized acceleration mirrors a gas pedal: more throttle = higher steam pressure = more torque.
        Layout follows the real schematic photo order: Condenser → Pistons → Oil Pan/Gen → Battery → Boiler.
    </p>
</div>

