    <h2 class="p10-section-title">1 Generator · 6-wheel + 2-rail torque coupling · pressurized throttle</h2>
    <p class="p10-section-lead">
        The hypothesis: steam pistons driving six wheels and two rail shafts produce enough combined
        torque to spin a single 200A / 48V generator — mounted directly on the oil pan — at sufficient
        RPM to output more than the 4.2 kW the immersion heater demands. If confirmed, six generators
        (Phase 9) produce massive surplus. This phase exists to validate the loop before scaling.
        Pressurized acceleration means the throttle valve controls steam admission pressure: low pedal =
        low PSI = idle torque; full pedal = 150 PSI = maximum torque and speed.
    </p>

