    <h2 class="p10-section-title">Pedal position → steam admission pressure → torque → speed</h2>
    <p class="p10-section-lead">
        Just like a gas engine's throttle plate controls airflow, Phase 10's throttle valve controls
        steam admission pressure. More pedal = wider valve = higher PSI entering the pistons =
        greater piston force = more torque = higher RPM and vehicle speed.
        The PCW controller reads pedal position at 100 Hz and adjusts the servo-actuated admission
        valve linearly between 20 PSI (idle) and 150 PSI (full throttle).
    </p>

